        "content": "<p>cc <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110087\">@Kim Morrison</span> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=inferInstanceAs#doc\">docs#inferInstanceAs</a> suggest testing with</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstanceAs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>but this fails with</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"ss\">`inferInstanceAs</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">failed</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">contains</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">metavariables</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 581449313,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1774377870
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>inferInstanceAs</code> now only works with an expected type. The fix is to use <code>(inferInstance : Inhabited Nat)</code></p>",
        "id": 581453965,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1774379267
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>instead, perhaps it should suggest <code>#synth</code>?</p>",
        "id": 581456068,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1774380021
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I suppose there is a chance that <code>inferInstanceAs</code> will become a proper term elaborator with its own name, which will make <code>inferInstanceAs</code> work again how it used to. If so, the doc-string is only temporarily wrong.</p>",
        "id": 581456528,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1774380198
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've updated the doc-string for <code>inferInstanceAs</code> in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/13115\">lean#13115</a>, explaining that it should only be used with an expected type. I'll make sure this gets into v4.29.0.</p>",
        "id": 581508469,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1774402564
    }
]